Track 2: "Did You Burn the Return Address?"
- Story & Context: Late on a rain-drenched Tuesday at the Marble Arch Odeon, apprentice projectionist Sean Devlin sat surrounded by heaps of uncollected cinema mail, clutching a grease-stained envelope that had arrived three months after his brother’s cargo vessel went down off the Hebrides. Rather than slit the wax seal, Sean routed his vintage fuzz pedal straight into a contact mic wedged beneath the rim of a down-tuned steel drum, locking into an obsessive, weeping ten-minute blues vibrato that rattled the teeth of the cleaning staff downstairs. With tears mixing into the graphite powder on his cheeks, he whispered hoarsely into an intercom mic routed through a tape echo, "The postman died five winters before you wrote."
